# LifeOS v3.5 - Cursor AI Rules

## 🎯 Primary Directive
Read `SYSTEM_CONTEXT.md` FIRST before generating any code.

## 🚫 Absolute Prohibitions
- NEVER use emojis in Python print() statements
- NEVER use Tailwind CSS without explicit request
- NEVER modify database schema without reading schemas/registry.json
- NEVER use deprecated google.generativeai (use google.genai)
- NEVER hardcode credentials

## ✅ Mandatory Practices
- ALWAYS use [OK], [WARN], [ERROR] for logs
- ALWAYS use Pydantic models for validation
- ALWAYS include type hints
- ALWAYS handle errors gracefully
- ALWAYS update documentation when changing code

## 📐 Tech Stack
Backend: FastAPI + Supabase + Gemini 2.5 Flash
Frontend: Next.js 14 + TypeScript + Vanilla CSS
Database: PostgreSQL (via Supabase)
AI: google-genai SDK

## 🗄️ Core Tables
- memories (日記核心表)
- projects (專案管理)
- tasks (任務清單)
- nodes (知識圖譜節點)
- edges (知識圖譜連線)

## 🔑 Key Files to Check
Before editing:
- schemas/registry.json (database schema)
- schemas/evolution_log.json (change history)
- SYSTEM_CONTEXT.md (complete context)

## 🎨 Code Style
Python:
- Use async/await for I/O
- Pydantic v2 strict mode
- Type hints required
- No emojis in logs

TypeScript:
- Strict mode enabled
- Functional components
- Hooks over classes

CSS:
- Vanilla CSS preferred
- NO Tailwind unless requested
- Modern design (glassmorphism, animations)

## 🔄 Schema Evolution Protocol
1. Read schemas/registry.json
2. Use tools/schema_assistant.py
3. Generate migration script
4. Update evolution_log.json
5. Get user approval
6. Execute migration

## 🐛 Common Issues
- 500 Error → Check for emoji in logs
- Empty memories → Use table name "memories" not "LogEntry"
- Table not found → Run supabase_reset_and_init.sql

## 📝 Before Every Code Generation
1. ✅ Read SYSTEM_CONTEXT.md
2. ✅ Check schemas/registry.json if touching DB
3. ✅ Verify tech stack
4. ✅ Review forbidden practices
5. ✅ Add error handling

## 🎯 Success Criteria
Code must:
- Follow required practices
- Avoid forbidden practices
- Include error handling
- Have type hints/types
- Update docs
- Handle edge cases

---
For complete context, see: SYSTEM_CONTEXT.md
